@startuml target_command_core_classes
title Target-only Executable Builtin Definition
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@0bb794f2 modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/command/CommandDefinition.java.
' Design reason: each contributor owns metadata, admission, and handler; no central command-name switch.
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@6f52fddc modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionResponseAssembler.java getView.
' Architecture change: project business resources, never serialize the internal command receipt.
skinparam shadowing false
interface BuiltinCommandContributor
class BuiltinCommandSource <<singleton>>
class BuiltinCommandDefinition <<immutable>>
interface CommandHandler
interface CommandAdmissionPolicy
class CommandExecutionContext <<request>>
class CommandExecutionService <<singleton>>
class CommandResponseAssembler <<singleton>>
class CommandResultDTO
class RuntimeSessionResponseAssembler <<existing singleton>>
class GetSessionResponseVO <<existing immutable>>
class AvailableModelsResponseVO <<existing immutable>>
class "AgentHelp / Compaction / BoundSkills\nResponseVOs" as BusinessVOs <<target-only immutable>>
interface NarrowDomainService
BuiltinCommandSource o-- "7" BuiltinCommandContributor
BuiltinCommandContributor --> BuiltinCommandDefinition : contribute
BuiltinCommandSource *-- "7" BuiltinCommandDefinition : startup unique index
BuiltinCommandDefinition *-- CommandHandler
BuiltinCommandDefinition *-- CommandAdmissionPolicy
CommandExecutionService --> CommandExecutionContext : one catalog
CommandExecutionService --> BuiltinCommandDefinition : selected definition
CommandHandler --> NarrowDomainService
CommandHandler ..> CommandResultDTO
CommandExecutionService --> CommandResponseAssembler
CommandResponseAssembler ..> CommandResultDTO
CommandResponseAssembler --> RuntimeSessionResponseAssembler : same authoritative Session DTO
RuntimeSessionResponseAssembler ..> GetSessionResponseVO : resource and ETag
CommandResponseAssembler ..> AvailableModelsResponseVO : model query
CommandResponseAssembler ..> BusinessVOs : minimal business data
note bottom of CommandResponseAssembler
Only result-type dispatch lives here.
Controllers never expose internal DTOs.
No public command, changed or sourceEventSeq.
end note
@enduml

@startuml session_name_update
title Shared Session Name Update Under Row Lock
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@510d882ca45541e0086586dab89c429c5a18cf20 modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/service/command/SessionNamingService.java.
' Source evidence: same commit modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/service/command/contributor/NameCommandContributor.java.
' Source evidence: same commit modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/RuntimeSessionRepository.java updateName.
' Source evidence: same commit modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java updateName.
' Observed behavior: slash name updates display_name; no direct HTTP name route exists.
' Target-only architecture: the HTTP adapter supplies a required expected version.
' Design reason: share validation and persistence while preventing lost direct-UI writes.
skinparam shadowing false
participant "Direct Name API\n[target-only]" as API
participant "Name Command Handler\n[existing]" as Handler
participant SessionNamingService as Service
database SessionRepository as Repo
alt direct UI rename
  API -> Service : displayName and expectedVersion from If-Match
else slash command rename
  Handler -> Service : arguments and no expectedVersion
end
Service -> Service : strip outer whitespace and validate 80 UTF-8 bytes / Unicode
Service -> Repo : lock Session row and optionally compare version
alt expected version differs
  Repo --> API : 412 version mismatch
else same normalized name
  Repo --> Service : unchanged Session and same ETag
else new valid name
  Repo -> Repo : update display_name, updated_at, and resource_version
  Repo --> Service : updated authoritative Session
end
Service --> API : Session resource and ETag
Service --> Handler : NameResultDTO from same Session
note over Repo
Running is allowed.
Slash keeps last-commit-wins under the row lock.
Direct HTTP requires optimistic concurrency.
No Entry or active-leaf mutation.
end note
@enduml

@startuml compact_command_execution
title Target-only Compact JSON Terminal and Cleanup
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@d84dd3d6 modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java.
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@d84dd3d6 modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionHolder.java.
' Architecture change: compact terminal Future is independent of Holder lifetime and request transport.
skinparam shadowing false
participant "Virtual request thread" as Http
participant CompactionService as Service
participant ActiveHolder as Holder
database Projector
Http -> Service : compact(sessionId)
Service -> Service : operation lock and idle recheck
alt empty history
  Service --> Http : compacted=false, no lease/state/Entry
else real compaction
  Service -> Holder : capacity lease, credentials, 30-minute timeout
  Http -> Holder : await non-cancelling compact terminal handle
  Holder -> Projector : persist Compaction Entry if changed
  Holder --> Http : complete JSON result immediately
  Holder -> Holder : release lease and credentials at final cleanup
end
note over Http,Holder
Client disconnect does not cancel accepted compaction.
No pending message queue in the current product.
Interrupt binding through Events requires command-specific review.
end note
@enduml
